  "articleBody": "Deciding whether to repair or completely replace a damaged kitchen door frame can be a tough call. It often comes down to the extent and type of damage. If you're dealing with minor cosmetic issues like small dents, shallow scratches, or tiny splits, a simple repair can often bring your frame back to life. Think wood filler, sanding, and a fresh coat of paint. This is usually the quicker and more cost-effective option. However, if the frame is suffering from more severe problems like extensive rot, significant warping that affects the door's operation, or large structural cracks, replacement might be the better long-term solution. When a frame is badly compromised, repairing it might only be a temporary fix, and you could end up with recurring issues like a sticking door or poor insulation. Consider if the existing material can be matched too; sometimes, older frames are hard to blend new repairs into. If the damage is extensive or you're unsure about the best approach, getting a professional opinion can save you time and money in the long run. HH Remodeling LLC can help assess the situation and guide you on the best path forward for your Aurora home.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}